# Test: le's exit codes carry one meaning each, through the binary.
# accept-only: the registered native fixture builds the le personality and runs
# one line per meaning: usage errors (an unknown command, a namespace
# non-member, a stray word, a value outside an enum) answer 2; a commit check
# with no review answers 1; a gate with no checkout to read answers 3; a
# blocking hook answers the hook protocol's 2; a pass-through program's own
# failure passes through as its code; le help ai exit-codes names the
# exemptions.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-le-cli-usability AC-28 to AC-32 (D-Q8), through the product
# binary and its real composition root.
option=timeout:value=300s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/le-exit-codes
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
